SPDX LicenseRef definitions
===========================

The following project-specific SPDX identifiers are used in source-file
headers. They are local identifiers and are not entries in the SPDX License
List.


LicenseRef-PQClean-Public-Domain
--------------------------------

This identifier refers to the upstream PQClean designation used for the
ML-DSA and ML-KEM implementations:

    Public Domain (https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/public-domain/cc0/)

PQClean does not explicitly identify these implementations with the SPDX
license identifier CC0-1.0. This project therefore records the upstream
designation as a local LicenseRef instead of interpreting it as CC0-1.0.


LicenseRef-PQClean-HQC-Public-Domain
------------------------------------

This identifier refers to the upstream PQClean designation used for the HQC
implementation:

    Public Domain

The upstream PQClean repository does not provide a complete license text or
an explicit CC0 reference for HQC. This project therefore records the
upstream designation as a local LicenseRef instead of interpreting it as
CC0-1.0.


LicenseRef-PQClean-Support-Code-Public-Domain
-------------------------------------------------

This identifier refers to the public-domain FIPS-202 / Keccak and SHA-2
support code used by PQClean and adapted in this repository.

The original sources and authors are documented in the source comments and
in the FIPS-202 / Keccak and SHA-2 support code section below. No specific
SPDX License List identifier or explicit CC0 reference is asserted for these
original portions. This project therefore records the upstream designation
as a local LicenseRef.


ML-DSA / CRYSTALS-Dilithium
---------------------------

The original PQClean ML-DSA implementation, formerly known as
CRYSTALS-Dilithium, is identified in PQClean as:

    Public Domain

PQClean references the Creative Commons public-domain dedication:

    https://creativecommons.org/share-your-work/public-domain/cc0/

For the historical algorithm name used in this fork, the corresponding
source directory is ML_DSA/.


